<title>ARGENTINA: Banco Credito Argentino approves $100 mln bond.</title>
<headline>Banco Credito Argentino approves $100 mln bond.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine Banco Credito Argentino has approved a bond issue of up to $100 million, the bank said Thursday.</p>
<p>Banco Credito said in a statement to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange the bond will be a two-year issue and pay interest every six months. It did not say when the bond will be launched.</p>
<p>The bank added that the bond is part of the bank's $300 million medium-term bond program.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668</p>
</text>
